l":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coobenguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T00:58:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T00:58:34Z","body":"I feel this is related to a larger issue related to spotlight attenuation as a whole. This has always happened under certain conditions, not just after [#99136](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99136) and you may think that you can just turn up the attenuation to soften the edges, but no. If you try to soften the edges all it does is darken the entire spotlight so that the harsh line goes away. I should probably make a separate issue about this","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628643671/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628653722","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102241#issuecomment-2628653722","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102241","id":2628653722,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6crhKa","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-01T01:13:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T01:13:19Z","body":"> I feel this is related to a larger issue related to spotlight attenuation as a whole. This has always happened under certain conditions, not just after [#99136](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99136) and you may think that you can just turn up the attenuation to soften the edges, but no. If you try to soften the edges all it does is darken the entire spotlight so that the harsh line goes away. I should probably make a separate issue about this\n\nI think you are seeing a different issue. This one specifically came from a check we recently added where we just don't calculate the light when the attenuation is low enough. That code is brand new. \n\nIf you ran into a similar issue earlier, then it is a different issue. So please make a new bug report with a project that reproduces the issue you faced earlier and we can investigate it as well!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2628653722/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]